{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q161529","formula":"C₆H₄Cl₂","hill":"C6H4Cl2","elements":["H","C","Cl"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":4.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"1,4-dichlorobenzene","ru":"1,4-Дихлорбензол"},"descriptions":{"en":"1,4-Dichlorobenzene (1,4-DCB, p-DCB, or para-dichlorobenzene, sometimes abbreviated as PDCB or para) is an aryl chloride and isomer of dichlorobenzene with the formula C6H4Cl2. This colorless solid has a strong sweet odor reminiscent of mothballs. The molecule consists of a benzene ring with two chlorine atoms (replacing hydrogen atoms) on opposing sites of the ring.","ru":"1,4-Дихлорбензол (пара-дихлорбензол) — хлорорганическое ароматическое соединение, пара-изомер дихлорбензола с химической формулой C6H4Cl2. Представляет собой бесцветное твёрдое вещество с сильным запахом. Молекула состоит из бензольного кольца, где два атома водорода в пара-позиции заменены на два атома хлора."},"fame":26,"pubchemCid":4685,"mass":147.0,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=CC=C1Cl)Cl","inchikey":"OCJBOOLMMGQPQU-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,4-dichlorobenzene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"4685","atoms":12,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.116,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-3.116,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.395,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.395,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.698,"y":1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.697,"y":1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":0.697,"y":-1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.698,"y":-1.208,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.228,"y":2.157,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.228,"y":2.157,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":1.228,"y":-2.157,"z":0.0,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.228,"y":-2.157,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,2,1],[1,3,1],[2,4,2],[2,6,1],[3,5,2],[3,7,1],[4,5,1],[4,8,1],[5,9,1],[6,7,2],[6,10,1],[7,11,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url"